;; @also-unfused
;; Temporal plus or minus an integer (#1302).  DATE (I32 days), TIME (I32 ms)
;; and TIMESTAMP (I64 ns) move by a B8 / U8 / I16 / I32 / I64 count, the
;; integer on either side of +, and on the right of - (int - TIME is the one
;; int-minus-temporal pair).  The answer is the integer sum of the raw count
;; and the offset, wrapped to the temporal lane: a DATE or TIME keeps the low
;; 32 bits, a TIMESTAMP wraps in 64.  A null on either side is the temporal
;; null, and a sum that wraps onto the lane's null sentinel reads as null.
;; The vector forms run one typed pass (atomic_map_binary_op), and a query
;; lowers them to the DAG's integer + / - cast back to the temporal type
;; (dag_temporal_int_arith); every expectation below is the answer the boxed
;; per-element loop gave before either, and the query forms must equal the
;; vector ones, fused and unfused.
